      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait, what was that last sentence? \"This final line deepens the lore\"—is that part of the dialogue or was that just a note for me? \n\nAlso, it's moving in the right direction, but it's still coming in a bit light on the actual word count for a Major Quest. The engine is being really picky about the 'depth' threshold. If we can't get the word count up comfortably, the quest might get downgraded to a side quest in the build.\n\nI'm still holding firm on not wanting a bunch of repetitive \"darkness\" and \"shadows\" filler. But if you can flesh out the history of the Spire or the legends Silas heard as a boy to give it more weight, that would help. Just try to make it feel like a real, meaty piece of writing that hits that higher word count naturally.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
